In deference to the META post by Harry, which I think was meant to
relate to these posts, I will attempt to leave the "basics" of this
issue behind... and try to "add depth" by explaining how I believe
that the "minimal opportunity" as I refer to socialism, could be
realized in a market economy... without government intervention.

First... in a post from Krzys':
} Garrett Goebel makes some interesting comments on socialism, in
} particular claiming that it is created by capitalists who want to buy
} "social peace". This, I claim, is a very German perspective (and 
} I do not say it to imply any personal attacks, I just want to ask you all
